    intro="""The heartbeat shows up in the infrared light signal as a small repeating bump, about a tenth of a percent of the total. Rather than hunting for individual beats, which is fragile on a wrist, this code asks a different question: *at what time shift does the waveform best match a copy of itself?* That shift is the time between beats.""",
