        (5, 5, """`CONTACT_LEVEL`: the baseline must exceed 5000 counts to count as "against skin". With nothing covering the sensor the infrared baseline measured about 800 to 2,700; on skin it measured 130,000 to 170,000. 5000 sits safely between. A caveat from testing: the board lying face-down on a desk read about 7,600, above this level, so a desk can look like contact; the pulse amplitude check below then finds no pulse."""),
        (6, 6, """`MIN_AMPLITUDE`: the pulse must be at least 30 counts RMS (typical size). Uncovered, the noise measured about 11 counts; real wrist pulses measured 57 to 115, so 30 is a little over twice the noise."""),
