        (8, 9, """The range of beat periods searched, as shifts in samples: 40 to 150, which is 0.40 s to 1.50 s, or 150 down to 40 beats per minute. Shorter than 40 was tried and removed: at the very shortest shifts, slow drift matches itself well and produced false 182 bpm readings."""),
        (10, 10, """`MIN_CORRELATION`: how well the waveform must match itself (1.0 is a perfect copy, 0 is unrelated) to be believed. Scans that passed in the recordings scored 0.65 to 0.99: median 0.97 on the wrist trace with the strongest pulse, 0.94 on the fingertip and 0.77 on the strapped wrist. In the 60-second recording with no pulse, 5 of 57 scans scored above 0.65 by chance; those alone are never enough, because several scans in a row must agree."""),
        (11, 11, """`TIE_MARGIN`: if several shifts match nearly equally well (within 0.03), the shortest is taken. Needed because a waveform with a period of T also matches itself at 2T, sometimes slightly better."""),
